# Copy to .env.local (git ignores it) and fill in what you have. Nothing here is required
# to look things up — research, scans and the Terminal need no key at all.

# Coinbase CDP API key — SERVER-SIDE ONLY, both halves. It lets this app's own paid API
# (src/server/api.ts, GET /api/skills/<id>) collect x402 payments through Coinbase's
# facilitator (src/server/cdp.ts). Without it the API still lists and prices every skill but
# sells nothing, and says so. Create a key at portal.cdp.coinbase.com; the secret is either a
# base64 Ed25519 key or an EC key in PEM form (paste a PEM on one line with \n). Never VITE_.
CDP_API_KEY_ID=
CDP_API_KEY_SECRET=

# WalletConnect Project ID, from cloud.reown.com — ties the "Connect with
# WalletConnect" button to your own project. Public (it ends up in the client
# bundle), but still yours: register it, don't invent one. Leave blank and
# lib/connectors.ts throws a named error instead of calling the SDK with "".
# Client-side; must be prefixed VITE_ for Vite to expose it.
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# (The fee recipient is not an environment variable: it is CONTRACTS.treasury in
# src/config/chain.ts — set by the owner on 2026-09-30 — and every fee, the API's price
# included, is off while it is null.)
